        "Following the destruction of 'Ad, the Arab tribe of Thamud settled in the rugged rocky valley of Al-Hijr (now Madain Saleh in northwestern Saudi Arabia). Blessed with extraordinary architectural genius, they carved opulent, durable palaces directly out of the living sandstone cliffs: ﴿وَتَنْحِتُونَ مِنَ الْجِبَالِ بُيُوتًا فَارِهِينَ﴾ 'And you carve houses out of mountains with great skill.' (Surah Ash-Shu'ara 26:149).",
        "Yet material luxury led to moral rot. They worshipped stone idols and oppressed the destitute. To call them to justice, Allah raised Prophet Saleh, a respected youth known for his wisdom and integrity: ﴿وَإِلَىٰ ثَمُودَ أَخَاهُمْ صَالِحًا قَالَ يَا قَوْمِ اعْبُدُوا اللَّهَ مَا لَكُم مِّنْ إِلَٰهٍ غَيْرُهُ﴾ 'And to Thamud [We sent] their brother Saleh. He said, \"O my people, worship Allah; you have no deity other than Him.\"' (Surah Al-A'raf 7:73).",
        "Seeking to humiliate him publicly, the chieftains pointed to a massive, impenetrable boulder and demanded an impossible sign: 'Bring forth from this solid dead rock a pregnant she-camel of immense size!' Prophet Saleh extracted a solemn covenant that if Allah produced this miracle, they would immediately abandon their idols. Saleh stood in prayer, and suddenly the solid rock shook and split open, and a majestic, pregnant she-camel stepped forth alive, immediately giving birth to a healthy calf.",
        "Saleh warned them that this creature was a sacred sign belonging to Allah: ﴿هَٰذِهِ نَاقَةُ اللَّهِ لَكُمْ آيَةً فَذَرُوهَا تَأْكُلْ فِي أَرْضِ اللَّهِ وَلَا تَمَسُّوهَا بِسُوءٍ فَيَأْخُذَكُمْ عَذَابٌ أَلِيمٌ﴾ 'This is the she-camel of Allah [sent] to you as a sign. So leave her to eat within Allah's earth and do not touch her with harm, lest there seize you a painful punishment.' (Surah Al-A'raf 7:73). He instituted a strict rotation for water: ﴿قَالَ هَٰذِهِ نَاقَةٌ لَّهَا شِرْبٌ وَلَكُمْ شِرْبُ يَوْمٍ مَّعْلُومٍ﴾ (Surah Ash-Shu'ara 26:155); she drank all the water one day and provided rich milk for the whole town, leaving the spring to the townspeople the next day.",
        "Envious of the she-camel's popularity and the growing influence of Saleh, nine corrupt ringleaders conspired in the city: ﴿وَكَانَ فِي الْمَدِينَةِ تِسْعَةُ رَهْطٍ يُفْسِدُونَ فِي الْأَرْضِ وَلَا يُصْلِحُونَ﴾ (Surah An-Naml 27:48). Led by the most wretched criminal Qudar ibn Salif: ﴿إِذِ انبَعَثَ أَشْقَاهَا﴾ (Surah Ash-Shams 91:12), they ambushed the she-camel, shot arrows into her legs, and hamstrung her to death.",
        "Hearing of the atrocity, Prophet Saleh wept and declared the irrevocable divine verdict: ﴿فَقَالَ تَمَتَّعُوا فِي دَارِكُمْ ثَلَاثَةَ أَيَّامٍ ذَٰلِكَ وَعْدٌ غَيْرُ مَكْذُوبٍ﴾ 'Enjoy yourselves in your homes for three days. That is a promise not to be denied.' (Surah Hud 11:65). During those three days, the faces of the disbelievers turned yellow on the first day, blood-red on the second, and pitch-black on the third.",
        "At dawn of the fourth day, an ear-splitting blast (As-Sayhah) from the sky accompanied by a violent earthquake struck Al-Hijr: ﴿فَأَخَذَتْهُمُ الرَّجْفَةُ فَأَصْبَحُوا فِي دَارِهِمْ جَاثِمِينَ﴾ 'So the earthquake seized them, and they became within their home [corpses] fallen prone.' (Surah Al-A'raf 7:78). Prophet Saleh and the faithful were saved by Allah's grace, while the carved rock palaces became a silent graveyard."
