        "Prophet Dhul-Kifl is among the luminous prophets commemorated in the Holy Quran for unflinching steadfastness, moral reliability, and self-restraint. Allah pairs his name with towering figures of endurance: ﴿وَإِسْمَاعِيلَ وَإِدْرِيسَ وَذَا الْكِفْلِ كُلٌّ مِّنَ الصَّابِرِينَ * وَأَدْخَلْنَاهُمْ فِي رَحْمَتِنَا إِنَّهُم مِّنَ الصَّالِحِينَ﴾ 'And mention Ishmael, Idris, and Dhul-Kifl; all were of the patient. And We admitted them into Our mercy. Indeed, they were of the righteous.' (Surah Al-Anbiya 21:85-86).",
        "Scholars of prophetic chronicles, including Ibn Kathir, explain that his title 'Dhul-Kifl' translates literally as 'The Possessor of the Pledge' or 'The One Who Took Responsibility.' When the aging prophet of his time (identified by many commentators as Al-Yasa) sought a worthy successor to guide the people, he gathered the community and announced: 'Who among you will pledge to fast every single day, spend every night in voluntary prayer, and judge between people without ever losing his temper?'",
