        "Allah granted Dawud a remarkable physical miracle: iron was made completely soft and malleable in his bare hands, like wax or kneaded dough: ﴿وَأَلَنَّا لَهُ الْحَدِيدَ * أَنِ اعْمَلْ سَابِغَاتٍ وَقَدِّرْ فِي السَّرْدِ وَاعْمَلُوا صَالِحًا﴾ 'And We made pliable for him iron, [commanding him], \"Make full coats of mail and calculate [precisely] the links, and work [all of you] righteousness.\"' (Surah Saba 34:10-11). Instead of feeding upon royal taxes, Prophet Dawud ate solely from the manual labor of his own hands, weaving lightweight interlocking chainmail armor for soldiers.",
        "Prophet Muhammad (S.A.W.) praised Dawud as the ultimate model of balanced worship in Sahih Bukhari: 'The most beloved prayer to Allah is that of David, and the most beloved fast to Allah is that of David: he used to sleep half the night, pray for a third of it, and sleep for a sixth of it; and he used to fast on alternate days.'",
