        "Allah caused a gourd vine (Yaqtin) with broad sheltering leaves to sprout over him, providing cool shade and nourishing food while repelling flies until his strength returned: ﴿وَأَنبَتْنَا عَلَيْهِ شَجَرَةً مِّن يَقْطِينٍ﴾ (Surah As-Saffat 37:146). Meanwhile, in Nineveh, realizing their prophet had departed and seeing the dark omens of punishment, the entire population had repented with heartfelt tears, shedding their clothes and begging Allah for forgiveness. When Yunus returned, he found all one hundred thousand citizens united in pure monotheism—the only nation in history to avert divine chastisement through collective repentance."
