        "Beholding this divine omnipotence that creates outside biological seasons, hope ignited within Zakariyya's centenarian heart. He possessed no heir, his hair was snowy white, and his wife Elizabeth was elderly and barren. Slipping into the dark sanctuary at night, he raised a whisper-soft, deeply vulnerable prayer: ﴿إِذْ نَادَىٰ رَبَّهُ نِدَاءً خَفِيًّا * قَالَ رَبِّ إِنِّي وَهَنَ الْعَظْمُ مِنِّي وَاشْتَعَلَ الرَّأْسُ شَيْبًا وَلَمْ أَكُن بِدُعَائِكَ رَبِّ شَقِيًّا﴾ 'When he called to his Lord a private call: He said, \"My Lord, indeed my bones have grown weak, and my head has filled with white, and never have I been in my supplication to You, my Lord, unblessed.\"' (Surah Maryam 19:3-4).",
